CONFORMANCE.md §6.1, EVALUATION.md §1: a translated method no test calls has no receiver:
E9008, reported by check and build alike; the error blocks the C++ outputs.
-- project.canon --
project acme {
  canon: "0.1"
}
-- a/a.canon --
/// A.
package a

/// A healing potion.
record Potion {
  /// Hit points restored.
  heal: Int

  /// What a player missing missingHp gets back.
  export fn healFor(self, missingHp: Int) -> Int { return min(heal, max(missingHp, 0)) }
}

emit cpp { out: "out/", namespace: "acme::gen", mode: data }
-- build.txt --
error[E9008]  a/a.canon:10:13
  translated method Potion.healFor is called by no test of package a: add one, it gives the conformance test its receiver

1 error, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
